{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0119","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What is the name of the proposed domain adaptation method for neural machine translation, and what two approaches does it combine?","answer":"The method is called \"mixed fine tuning,\" and it combines fine tuning with multi domain NMT by training on out-of-domain data first, then fine tuning on a mix of in-domain and out-of-domain data."}
