{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0120","fact_refs":[0],"question":"By how much does the proposed dialog context language model outperform a conventional single-turn RNN language model, and on what dataset was this measured?","answer":"It outperforms the conventional single-turn RNN language model by 3.3% on perplexity, measured on the Switchboard Dialog Act Corpus."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0120","fact_refs":[1],"question":"How did Mikolov and Zweig construct the contextual vector for their topic-conditioned RNNLM?","answer":"They created the contextual vector by performing Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) on the preceding text."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0120","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What context representation methods did Wang and Cho explore for corpus-level discourse information in language modeling?","answer":"They explored bag-of-words, sequence of bag-of-words, and sequence of bag-of-words with attention."}
