{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0120","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What novel information did Tran et al.'s contextual language model take into account, and how did it improve performance?","answer":"Tran et al.'s model considered information at the inter-document level by utilizing structural information from a tree-structured document set, which largely improved language modeling performance."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0120","fact_refs":[5],"question":"Which RNN variant is widely used for language modeling because of its ability to capture longer term dependencies?","answer":"Long short-term memory (LSTM) is the widely used RNN variant noted for capturing longer term dependencies."}
